<!-- PROCESS -->
<section class="section" id="process">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">06 / THE ASTROVYN METHOD</div>
      <h2>Think clearly.<br><span class="accent">Build thoughtfully.</span></h2>
      <p>We aim to make the journey from curiosity to a shareable result structured, transparent, and open to improvement.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="process-grid">
      <article class="process-card reveal">
        <div class="process-num">STEP / 01</div>
        <h3>Question</h3>
        <p>Start with a meaningful problem. Define what you want to know, why it matters, and what a useful answer might look like.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="process-card reveal delay-1">
        <div class="process-num">STEP / 02</div>
        <h3>Investigate</h3>
        <p>Read, compare, calculate, and learn from credible sources. Separate established findings from hypotheses and speculation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="process-card reveal delay-2">
        <div class="process-num">STEP / 03</div>
        <h3>Develop</h3>
        <p>Translate knowledge into a design, model, experiment, simulation, or digital prototype suited to the question.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="process-card reveal delay-3">
        <div class="process-num">STEP / 04</div>
        <h3>Share</h3>
        <p>Document the process, explain the outcome, acknowledge limitations, and make the work available for feedback and further learning.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PRINCIPLES -->
<section class="section" id="principles">
  <div class="container principles">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">07 / WHAT GUIDES US</div>
      <div class="principle-quote">“The goal is not to appear knowledgeable. <span>The goal is to understand more than we did yesterday.</span>”</div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle-list reveal delay-1">
      <div class="principle-item">
        <div class="sym">✳</div>
        <div><h4>Curiosity without boundaries</h4><p>Important questions often emerge between disciplines. We stay open to unfamiliar ideas and perspectives.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-item">
        <div class="sym">⌖</div>
        <div><h4>Evidence before assumptions</h4><p>We value reliable information, transparent reasoning, and honest acknowledgment of uncertainty.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-item">
        <div class="sym">↗</div>
        <div><h4>Progress through iteration</h4><p>First attempts are opportunities to learn. Feedback, testing, and revision make ideas stronger.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-item">
        <div class="sym">◎</div>
        <div><h4>Knowledge worth sharing</h4><p>Clear explanations and responsible documentation help others understand, question, and build on our work.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-item">
        <div class="sym">◇</div>
        <div><h4>Responsible innovation</h4><p>We consider safety, ethics, limitations, and potential consequences alongside technical possibility.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ROADMAP -->
<section class="section roadmap-section" id="roadmap">
