      <p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:8px">Building ASTROVYN around research, exploration, and innovation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="founder-content reveal delay-1">
      <div class="eyebrow">10 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE INITIATIVE</div>
      <h3>Built on curiosity.<br><span class="accent">Driven by possibility.</span></h3>
      <p>ASTROVYN is founded by Ansh Srivastava, a Class 11 student and JEE aspirant interested in science, space exploration, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies.</p>
      <p>The motivation behind ASTROVYN is to create a place where curiosity can grow into research, research can lead to project ideas, and project ideas can be explored through learning, experimentation, and thoughtful development.</p>
      <p>The aim is not to claim that every idea is a breakthrough. It is to create a consistent process for learning deeply, asking better questions, building skills, and sharing progress with the world.</p>
      <div class="founder-note">“There is always more to explore, more to understand, and something new to create.”</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">11 / FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</div>
      <h2>Get to know <span class="accent">ASTROVYN.</span></h2>
      <p>A few answers about the purpose, interests, and direction of the community.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What exactly is ASTROVYN?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>ASTROVYN is an independent research and innovation community focused on exploring scientific concepts, investigating emerging technologies, and developing educational projects and ideas. It is an evolving initiative rather than a claim to be a formal scientific institution.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What topics does ASTROVYN explore?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Our areas of interest include space science, astronomy, artificial intelligence, robotics, rocket propulsion theory, quantum physics, scientific computing, energy systems, engineering, and future technology.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Are the projects shown on this website completed?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The project cards currently describe possible project concepts. They should not be interpreted as completed, tested, or independently validated projects. As actual work is developed, its status, documentation, and results can be added honestly.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Does ASTROVYN only focus on space science?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Space science is an important interest, but ASTROVYN also explores AI, robotics, physics, energy, scientific computing, engineering, and other technology-related fields. The goal is to connect ideas across disciplines.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>How can I suggest an idea or collaboration?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Use the contact section below to send a message about a research question, project concept, learning resource, or potential collaboration. Include enough detail to explain what you would like to explore.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Does ASTROVYN provide official scientific certification?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. ASTROVYN is an independent community initiative. Information and projects should be evaluated on the quality of their sources, methodology, documentation, and evidence rather than on any claim of official certification.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What is the meaning behind the tagline?</span><span>+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>“Converting Curiosity Into Innovations” describes the journey from asking questions to learning, researching, developing concepts, and working toward practical outcomes. It expresses the community's direction and ambition.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

